# Changelogs

One folder per repo, one file per day. Every Claude Code session that changes a repo appends to (or creates) `changelog/<repo>/YYYY-MM-DD.md` at the end of the change.

| Repo | Folder |
|---|---|
{changelog_rows}

## File format

Filename: `YYYY-MM-DD.md`, the date the change was made, in local time. If the file already exists for that day, append a new entry. Never overwrite earlier entries.

```markdown
# {today}

## HH:MM — <short title of the change>

**Scope:** <module or area touched, e.g. `billing`, `apps/admin`>
**Type:** feature | fix | refactor | chore | docs | test
**Design doc:** design/<feature>/... (if any)

### What changed
- One bullet per meaningful change, with file paths (`src/billing/invoice.py`).

### Why
- One or two lines of motivation, or the ticket.

### How to verify
- Commands run, tests added or updated, manual steps.

### Follow-ups / risks
- Migrations or commands to run on deploy, permissions to update, the impact on other repos, breaking API changes for clients.
```

## Rules

- One entry per logical change, not per file. A change that spans repos gets an entry in each repo's file.
- Always state the impact on other repos (an API change a client consumes, a permission name a frontend checks, data that syncs between services), or say there is none.
- Never paste secrets, tokens or `.env` values.
- Keep entries short. Link the design doc for detail.
- Two people can append to the same day's file. `.gitattributes` at the hub root merges these files with `merge=union`, so both entries are kept.
